// 1000 Cuts (v2.1.0, 25 Oct 2026): a dated chronology of the Williams family's position at Great House Farm in law and in fact,
// 1870s-1988. Each entry: date, event, what changed (cited), label, evidence links, depends-on/enabled cross-links, open question.
// Editorial rule (ingredients, not conclusions): no stated conclusion, no drawn pyramid; the closing lists what was decided, what was
// never decided, what the courts found against the family, and open questions, then competing theories ranked most to least plausible (the courts' view ranked with the rest). Data: work/thousand-cuts/cuts.v2.json. — Sion's Tab agent
export const THOUSAND_CUTS_PAGES = {"/timeline/thousand-cuts/": {"title": "1000 Cuts: a dated chronology of the Williams family at Great House Farm (1870s–1988)", "html": "<style>.tc{--tc-line:rgba(127,127,127,.35);--tc-soft:rgba(127,127,127,.08);--tc-rec:#2e7d32;--tc-tes:#6a1b9a;--tc-nyc:#8d6e00;max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.55;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n.tc *{box-sizing:border-box}.tc h2{margin:1.6em 0 .4em;font-size:1.25em;border-bottom:1px solid var(--tc-line);padding-bottom:.2em}\n.tc .lede{font-size:1.05em}.tc .muted{opacity:.75;font-size:.92em}.tc nav.yrs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px;margin:.6em 0}.tc nav.yrs a{font-size:.82em;padding:2px 8px;border:1px solid var(--tc-line);border-radius:10px;text-decoration:none}\n.tc .cut{border:1px solid var(--tc-line);border-radius:8px;padding:.6em .75em;margin:.6em 0;scroll-margin-top:90px}.tc .cut.ctx{border-style:dashed}\n.tc .cut .hd{display:flex;gap:.5em;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap}.tc .cid{font-weight:700;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:.9em}.tc .dt{font-weight:600}\n.tc .ev{margin:.3em 0}.tc .chg{margin:.35em 0;padding:.35em .55em;background:var(--tc-soft);border-radius:6px}.tc .opn{margin:.35em 0;font-size:.9em;font-style:italic}\n.tc .refs a,.tc .deps a{display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:1px 7px;border:1px solid var(--tc-line);border-radius:10px;font-size:.82em;text-decoration:none}.tc .xd{opacity:.7}\n.tc .deps{font-size:.88em;margin-top:.3em}.tc .lab{font-size:.75em;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid currentColor;white-space:nowrap}\n.tc .l-rec{color:var(--tc-rec)}.tc .l-tes{color:var(--tc-tes)}.tc .l-nyc{color:var(--tc-nyc)}.tc .l-inf{color:#1565c0}.tc ul.tight{padding-left:1.2em}.tc ul.tight li{margin:.3em 0}\n@media (max-width:420px){.tc{font-size:15px}}</style>\n<div class=\"tc\" id=\"tc-top\">\n<p class=\"lede\">A dated chronology of the Williams family&#x27;s position at Great House Farm in law and in fact, 1870s to 1988, each step linked to its evidence.</p>\n<p>Each entry gives a date, what happened, what it changed in law or in fact, and the evidence pages it rests on. &quot;Depends on&quot; and &quot;Enabled&quot; link each entry to the earlier entries it built on and the later ones that built on it. Open both ends of a link to check it.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Record = read in a court judgment, registry, archive, legislation or contemporaneous press. Family testimony = the family&#x27;s own account. Not yet confirmed = no source located yet. Open question = what the record does not yet answer, and what would answer it.</p>\n<nav class=\"yrs\" aria-label=\"Periods\"><a href=\"#period-0\">1870s–1939</a><a href=\"#period-1\">1916–1940</a><a href=\"#period-2\">1945–1954</a><a href=\"#period-3\">1955–1965</a><a href=\"#period-4\">1966–1972</a><a href=\"#period-5\">1974</a><a href=\"#period-6\">1975</a><a href=\"#period-7\">1982–1983</a><a href=\"#period-8\">1984–1987</a><a href=\"#period-9\">1988</a><a href=\"#after\">After 1988</a><a href=\"#ingredients\">Decided and undecided</a><a href=\"#theories\">Theories</a></nav>\n<h2 id=\"period-0\">1870s–1939: the family at Great House Farm</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p1\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P1</span><span class=\"dt\">1870s–1916</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names him; the 1904 Bute rent audit lists him &quot;of Llandough Farm&quot;.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> On paper, the occupation is a tenancy from the Bute estate: the 1904 rent audit <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0227-cardiff-times-1904-john-williams-tenancy-since-1855/\">EV-0227</a> and the Feb 1916 tenancy with plan <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a> both name John Williams as tenant.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0227-cardiff-times-1904-john-williams-tenancy-since-1855/\">EV-0227</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Enabled: <a href=\"#c01\" title=\"Feb 1916 · Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.\">C01 <span class=\"xd\">Feb 1916</span></a> <a href=\"#c06\" title=\"c.1950–52 · Family title papers removed from the farmhouse blanket box.\">C06 <span class=\"xd\">c.1950–52</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p2\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P2</span><span class=\"dt\">May 1897</span><span class=\"lab l-nyc\">Not yet confirmed</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Marconi&#x27;s wireless tests at Lavernock and Flat Holm, close by. Family tradition holds that he stayed at the farm.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The 1897 press and the extracts of Kemp&#x27;s diary record the tests at Lavernock and Flat Holm <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0011-marconi-lavernock-wireless-cutting-1897/\">EV-0011</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0248-marconi-in-wales-may-1897-contemporary-press/\">EV-0248</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0256-kemp-diary-lavernock-1897-bodleian-ms-marconi-89/\">EV-0256</a>; none of the extracts read so far names Great House Farm.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0011-marconi-lavernock-wireless-cutting-1897/\">EV-0011</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0248-marconi-in-wales-may-1897-contemporary-press/\">EV-0248</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0256-kemp-diary-lavernock-1897-bodleian-ms-marconi-89/\">EV-0256</a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Did the Marconi team stay at the farm? The full Kemp diary (Bodleian MS. Marconi 89) or a letter placing the team there would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p3\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P3</span><span class=\"dt\">1890s (year not yet found)</span><span class=\"lab l-nyc\">Not yet confirmed</span></div><div class=\"ev\">&quot;Peerless&quot; Jim Driscoll&#x27;s first fight in the farm barn.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> A local-history summary places the fight in the farm barn <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0009-family-tree-planting-parcel-a/\">EV-0009</a>; the year and the National Monuments Record citation have not been located.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0009-family-tree-planting-parcel-a/\">EV-0009</a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> When was the fight, and what is the primary source? A dated report or the NMR entry would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p4\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P4</span><span class=\"dt\">1891 to 1955</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Trees planted on Parcel A, the house parcel, in view of the town: one of the family&#x27;s acts of occupation.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The family&#x27;s account of tree planting on Parcel A, with an undated photograph <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0009-family-tree-planting-parcel-a/\">EV-0009</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0199-photograph-tree-planting-at-great-house-farm-date/\">EV-0199</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0009-family-tree-planting-parcel-a/\">EV-0009</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0199-photograph-tree-planting-at-great-house-farm-date/\">EV-0199</a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What did the planting cover, and when? Dated photographs, aerial images or survey sheets would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p5\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P5</span><span class=\"dt\">1928</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Last rent for the house parcel paid in 1928, when the quarry machinery left; no rent for the house parcel after that.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The family&#x27;s account <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a>; no receipt for 1928 has been located. The Court of Appeal recorded rent arrears in the mid-1930s and late 1940s and a last payment, under a judgment for arrears, in 1953 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Which is right for the house parcel: rent ending in 1928, or arrears and a 1953 payment? A rent book or the 1953 judgment file would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p6\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P6</span><span class=\"dt\">1928 to 1949</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">No one takes issue with the stopped rent for about twenty years, until the 1949 surrender and re-grant (family account).</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The family&#x27;s account <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a>. The judgment gives arrears &quot;in the mid-1930s and in the late 1940s&quot; as the background to the 1949 arrangement <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0025-frederick-buckler-unwritten-tenancy-1949/\">EV-0025</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0025-frederick-buckler-unwritten-tenancy-1949/\">EV-0025</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p7\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P7</span><span class=\"dt\">1939</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The 1939 Western Ground Rents agreement plan shows the fields (Parcel B) only, highlighted; the house parcel is not shown on it.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The plan to the 1939 Western Ground Rents agreement highlights the fields (Parcel B) and does not show the house parcel <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0023-1939-wgr-john-williams-tenancy-plan/\">EV-0023</a>. Page 1 of the agreement is not yet held.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0023-1939-wgr-john-williams-tenancy-plan/\">EV-0023</a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What does page 1 of the 1939 agreement describe as let?</div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-1\">1916–1940</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c01\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C01</span><span class=\"dt\">Feb 1916</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The family&#x27;s occupation is put in writing as a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a>. The Court of Appeal opens its account of the facts with this letting <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#p1\" title=\"1870s–1916 · John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names him;\">P1 <span class=\"xd\">1870s–1916</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance later b\">C02 <span class=\"xd\">23–25 Dec 1938</span></a> <a href=\"#c04\" title=\"mid-1930s and late 1940s · The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.\">C04 <span class=\"xd\">mid-1930s and late 1940s</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c02\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C02</span><span class=\"dt\">23–25 Dec 1938</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance later becomes the root of title.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The reversion passes from the Bute estate to Western Ground Rents Ltd <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0019-bute-wgr-conveyance-plan-1938/\">EV-0019</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0022-press-1938-bute-wgr-sale-completion/\">EV-0022</a>; this conveyance later serves as the root of title in the chain that leads to BP <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0216-1965-contract-condition-f-conveyance-25-december-1938/\">EV-0216</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0019-bute-wgr-conveyance-plan-1938/\">EV-0019</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0022-press-1938-bute-wgr-sale-completion/\">EV-0022</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0216-1965-contract-condition-f-conveyance-25-december-1938/\">EV-0216</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c01\" title=\"Feb 1916 · Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.\">C01 <span class=\"xd\">Feb 1916</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c04\" title=\"mid-1930s and late 1940s · The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.\">C04 <span class=\"xd\">mid-1930s and late 1940s</span></a> <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July\">C10 <span class=\"xd\">1955 and 4 Jul 1955</span></a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15 <span class=\"xd\">31 Dec 1969</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Was the farmhouse parcel inside the 1938 conveyance and plan? The conveyance and plan would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c03\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C03</span><span class=\"dt\">1 Jul 1940</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession must be &quot;adverse&quot;; s.13 a formal entry alone keeps nothing alive).</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> From 1 July 1940, 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner&#x27;s claim (s.10 requires the possession to be &quot;adverse&quot;; under s.13 a formal entry alone does not stop the clock). The 1987 judgment applies this Act to every later step <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Enabled: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Fred\">C05 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1949</span></a> <a href=\"#c07\" title=\"1953 · Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.\">C07 <span class=\"xd\">1953</span></a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a> <a href=\"#c18\" title=\"3 Jul 1974 · BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under th\">C18 <span class=\"xd\">3 Jul 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforced from \">C19 <span class=\"xd\">17–19 Sep 1974</span></a></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-2\">1945–1954</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c04\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C04</span><span class=\"dt\">mid-1930s and late 1940s</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The courts treat the unpaid rent as arrears under a continuing tenancy, not as the end of the tenancy <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. The family&#x27;s account dates the end of rent to 1928 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c01\" title=\"Feb 1916 · Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.\">C01 <span class=\"xd\">Feb 1916</span></a> <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance later b\">C02 <span class=\"xd\">23–25 Dec 1938</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Fred\">C05 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1949</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c05\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C05</span><span class=\"dt\">2 Feb 1949</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Frederick Buckler. It is never put in writing.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The tenancy passes from John Williams to Frederick Buckler as a new yearly tenancy, never put in writing <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0025-frederick-buckler-unwritten-tenancy-1949/\">EV-0025</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. The occupier is now a tenant of the 1949 grant.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0025-frederick-buckler-unwritten-tenancy-1949/\">EV-0025</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c04\" title=\"mid-1930s and late 1940s · The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.\">C04 <span class=\"xd\">mid-1930s and late 1940s</span></a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession must \">C03 <span class=\"xd\">1 Jul 1940</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c07\" title=\"1953 · Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.\">C07 <span class=\"xd\">1953</span></a> <a href=\"#c08\" title=\"1954 · A further attempt to treat Frederick Buckler as a tenant.\">C08 <span class=\"xd\">1954</span></a> <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1955</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Why was the 1949 re-grant made, and on whose initiative? Estate correspondence from 1948–49 would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c06\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C06</span><span class=\"dt\">c.1950–52</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Family title papers removed from the farmhouse blanket box.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The family&#x27;s account: the title papers kept in the farmhouse blanket box were removed <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0026-family-title-papers-removed-blanket-box/\">EV-0026</a>. No court record mentions them.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0026-family-title-papers-removed-blanket-box/\">EV-0026</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#p1\" title=\"1870s–1916 · John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names him;\">P1 <span class=\"xd\">1870s–1916</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What were the papers, and where are they now?</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c07\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C07</span><span class=\"dt\">1953</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> A rent payment made under a county-court judgment for arrears <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0030-cardiff-county-court-registers-aca/\">EV-0030</a>. In law a payment of rent acknowledges the landlord&#x27;s title, so no 12-year period runs before it.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0030-cardiff-county-court-registers-aca/\">EV-0030</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Fred\">C05 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1949</span></a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession must \">C03 <span class=\"xd\">1 Jul 1940</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1955</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c08\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C08</span><span class=\"dt\">1954</span><span class=\"lab l-nyc\">Not yet confirmed</span></div><div class=\"ev\">A further attempt to treat Frederick Buckler as a tenant.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> A further step treating Frederick Buckler as a tenant is listed in the family record <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0031-1954-buckler-tenancy-attempt/\">EV-0031</a>; its source has not been located.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0031-1954-buckler-tenancy-attempt/\">EV-0031</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Fred\">C05 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1949</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What happened in 1954? The source document would answer it.</div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-3\">1955–1965</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c09\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C09</span><span class=\"dt\">2 Feb 1955</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The tenancy ends; Frederick Buckler stays on without one. The Court of Appeal held that Frederick and Mary were in adverse possession of the house and garden from this date <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Fred\">C05 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1949</span></a> <a href=\"#c07\" title=\"1953 · Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.\">C07 <span class=\"xd\">1953</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July\">C10 <span class=\"xd\">1955 and 4 Jul 1955</span></a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c10\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C10</span><span class=\"dt\">1955 and 4 Jul 1955</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July 1955: all the farm is taken except the farmhouse and garden.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The High Court order is enforced on 4 July 1955 and every part of the farm except the farmhouse and garden is taken into possession <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0032-1955-order-14-possession-order/\">EV-0032</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0034-writ-possession-execution-return-1955/\">EV-0034</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. The family records that Mary had just had a leg amputated and refused to leave <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0034-writ-possession-execution-return-1955/\">EV-0034</a>. The order itself is not yet located.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0032-1955-order-14-possession-order/\">EV-0032</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0034-writ-possession-execution-return-1955/\">EV-0034</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1955</span></a> <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance later b\">C02 <span class=\"xd\">23–25 Dec 1938</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c11\" title=\"1958 · Leckwith Common inquiry and Glamorgan County Council acquisitions near the farm; Mary&#x27;s &quot;Crichel Down&quot; objecti\">C11 <span class=\"xd\">1958</span></a> <a href=\"#c12\" title=\"1959 and Mar 1965 · Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing is offere\">C12 <span class=\"xd\">1959 and Mar 1965</span></a> <a href=\"#c16\" title=\"16 Jun 1970 · Village green VG41 registered by Glamorgan County Council.\">C16 <span class=\"xd\">16 Jun 1970</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What exactly did the 1955 order cover? The High Court order would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c11\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C11</span><span class=\"dt\">1958</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Leckwith Common inquiry and Glamorgan County Council acquisitions near the farm; Mary&#x27;s &quot;Crichel Down&quot; objection goes no further, and no petition is presented in Parliament.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Land near the farm passes into public schemes after the Leckwith Common inquiry <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0035-western-mail-1958-leckwith-common-hearing/\">EV-0035</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0036-western-mail-1958-gcc-acquisition-notice/\">EV-0036</a>. Mary&#x27;s &quot;Crichel Down&quot; objection is recorded <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0037-western-mail-1958-crichel-down/\">EV-0037</a>; no petition was presented in Parliament <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0038-hansard-1958-leckwith-common-no-petition/\">EV-0038</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0035-western-mail-1958-leckwith-common-hearing/\">EV-0035</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0036-western-mail-1958-gcc-acquisition-notice/\">EV-0036</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0037-western-mail-1958-crichel-down/\">EV-0037</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0038-hansard-1958-leckwith-common-no-petition/\">EV-0038</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July\">C10 <span class=\"xd\">1955 and 4 Jul 1955</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What became of the 1958 objection? The inquiry file would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c12\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C12</span><span class=\"dt\">1959 and Mar 1965</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing is offered and refused.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Tenancy and housing offers are made and refused <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0039-wgr-tenancy-offers-1959-1965/\">EV-0039</a>. In 1986 the trial judge relied on the March 1965 offer in finding that Frederick had no intention to possess as owner <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0039-wgr-tenancy-offers-1959-1965/\">EV-0039</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July\">C10 <span class=\"xd\">1955 and 4 Jul 1955</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c13\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C13</span><span class=\"dt\">11 Dec 1962</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profits; a suspended committal order against Frederick Buckler follows in June 1963.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> A court orders possession of the farmhouse and garden <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0030-cardiff-county-court-registers-aca/\">EV-0030</a>. The Court of Appeal held that this order stopped the 12-year period before it had run, so the owner&#x27;s title was not extinguished <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. The order was not enforced until leave was sought in 1974.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0030-cardiff-county-court-registers-aca/\">EV-0030</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1955</span></a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession must \">C03 <span class=\"xd\">1 Jul 1940</span></a> <a href=\"#c12\" title=\"1959 and Mar 1965 · Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing is offere\">C12 <span class=\"xd\">1959 and Mar 1965</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c14\" title=\"1965–67 · Frederick Buckler dies. Mary stays in the house.\">C14 <span class=\"xd\">1965–67</span></a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15 <span class=\"xd\">31 Dec 1969</span></a> <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforced from \">C19 <span class=\"xd\">17–19 Sep 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-4\">1966–1972</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c14\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C14</span><span class=\"dt\">1965–67</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Frederick Buckler dies. Mary stays in the house.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Mary remains the occupier. The trial judge held that, while Frederick lived, only his intention counted <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c15\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C15</span><span class=\"dt\">31 Dec 1969</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The paper title, and as successor the benefit of the 1962 order, passes to BP Pension Trust <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0043-wgr-bp-pension-trust-conveyance/\">EV-0043</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0043-wgr-bp-pension-trust-conveyance/\">EV-0043</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance later b\">C02 <span class=\"xd\">23–25 Dec 1938</span></a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c17\" title=\"1972 · Outline planning permission for about 13 houses, with an ownership certificate.\">C17 <span class=\"xd\">1972</span></a> <a href=\"#c18\" title=\"3 Jul 1974 · BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under th\">C18 <span class=\"xd\">3 Jul 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforced from \">C19 <span class=\"xd\">17–19 Sep 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and sewer \">C22 <span class=\"xd\">23 May 1975</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c16\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C16</span><span class=\"dt\">16 Jun 1970</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Village green VG41 registered by Glamorgan County Council.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> A village green, VG41, is registered by the county council <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\">EV-0044</a>. The certified map shows a small roadside wedge <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0263-commons-registration-1965-publicity-glamorgan-notices-vg41/\">EV-0263</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\">EV-0044</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0263-commons-registration-1965-publicity-glamorgan-notices-vg41/\">EV-0263</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July\">C10 <span class=\"xd\">1955 and 4 Jul 1955</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c28\" title=\"26 Jul 1983 (in force 1 Sep 1983) · The Commons Registration (Glamorgan) Act 1983 validates the Glamorgan common-land registers.\">C28 <span class=\"xd\">26 Jul 1983 (in force 1 Sep 1983)</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Does VG41 overlap the house parcel? An overlay of the certified map on the 1916 plan would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c17\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C17</span><span class=\"dt\">1972</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Outline planning permission for about 13 houses, with an ownership certificate.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Outline permission for about 13 houses is granted on an application carrying an ownership certificate <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0046-1972-outline-planning-permission-ownership-certificate/\">EV-0046</a>. The site is now on the planning register as a development site.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0046-1972-outline-planning-permission-ownership-certificate/\">EV-0046</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15 <span class=\"xd\">31 Dec 1969</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Who signed the 1972 ownership certificate, and was the occupier notified? The planning file would answer it.</div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-5\">1974</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c18\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C18</span><span class=\"dt\">3 Jul 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under the 1939 Act. The action is adjourned part-heard and &quot;has never been finally heard&quot;.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under the 1939 Act. The action is adjourned part-heard and, in the Court of Appeal&#x27;s words, &quot;has never been finally heard&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. No decision on that plea is on the record.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15 <span class=\"xd\">31 Dec 1969</span></a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession must \">C03 <span class=\"xd\">1 Jul 1940</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What does the 1974 court file show was pleaded and left undecided? The HMCTS reply due 2 Nov 2026 would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c19\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C19</span><span class=\"dt\">17–19 Sep 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforced from 31 Oct 1974. She appeals, saying she had too little notice to be heard.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Leave is given to execute the 1962 order, enforceable from 31 Oct 1974 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>; the 12-year period from that order would have ended on 11 Dec 1974. Her appeal raised too little notice to be heard.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15 <span class=\"xd\">31 Dec 1969</span></a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession must \">C03 <span class=\"xd\">1 Jul 1940</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c20\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C20</span><span class=\"dt\">31 Oct 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for life: &quot;no proceedings will be commenced until you personally no longer live there&quot;.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The letters permit her to stay rent-free for life <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0048-telegraph-open-day-ancient-house/\">EV-0048</a>. The Court of Appeal held that from then on her possession was &quot;by the licence of BP Properties&quot; and no longer adverse <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0048-telegraph-open-day-ancient-house/\">EV-0048</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforced from \">C19 <span class=\"xd\">17–19 Sep 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c18\" title=\"3 Jul 1974 · BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under th\">C18 <span class=\"xd\">3 Jul 1974</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c21\" title=\"Nov–Dec 1974 · On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not reject\">C21 <span class=\"xd\">Nov–Dec 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and sewer \">C22 <span class=\"xd\">23 May 1975</span></a> <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive.\">C25 <span class=\"xd\">23 Feb 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c26\" title=\"26 Mar 1983 · Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).\">C26 <span class=\"xd\">26 Mar 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29 <span class=\"xd\">May 1984</span></a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c21\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C21</span><span class=\"dt\">Nov–Dec 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not reject the letters.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The Court of Appeal recorded that she did not reject the letters: &quot;she did not, however, do that&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a>. The court treated that as accepting the licence.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Did Mary or her solicitors write after 31 Oct 1974 rejecting the licence? Such a letter would meet the point the Court of Appeal identified.</div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-6\">1975</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c22\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C22</span><span class=\"dt\">23 May 1975</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and sewer rights &quot;to serve any development&quot;.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The farmhouse plot passes from BP Pension Trust to BP Properties, with 80-year road and sewer rights reserved &quot;to serve any development&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0052-bp-pension-trust-bp-properties-conveyance/\">EV-0052</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0052-bp-pension-trust-bp-properties-conveyance/\">EV-0052</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15 <span class=\"xd\">31 Dec 1969</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required within two \">C24 <span class=\"xd\">19 and 30 Nov 1982</span></a> <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive.\">C25 <span class=\"xd\">23 Feb 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29 <span class=\"xd\">May 1984</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c23\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C23</span><span class=\"dt\">1 Dec 1975</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Vale of Glamorgan becomes a compulsory registration area.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> First registration becomes compulsory on sale in the Vale of Glamorgan <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0265-hmlr-registration-background-compulsory-1975-r29-certificate/\">EV-0265</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0265-hmlr-registration-background-compulsory-1975-r29-certificate/\">EV-0265</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Enabled: <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required within two \">C24 <span class=\"xd\">19 and 30 Nov 1982</span></a> <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive.\">C25 <span class=\"xd\">23 Feb 1983</span></a></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-7\">1982–1983</h2>\n<div class=\"cut ctx\" id=\"c24\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C24</span><span class=\"dt\">19 and 30 Nov 1982</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required within two months.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered as WA231076 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0059-wa231076-form-a13-first-registration/\">EV-0059</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0071-wa231076-1983-84-registration-activity/\">EV-0071</a>. After this the farmhouse is the only unregistered part of the BP holding at the farm.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0059-wa231076-form-a13-first-registration/\">EV-0059</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0071-wa231076-1983-84-registration-activity/\">EV-0071</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and sewer \">C22 <span class=\"xd\">23 May 1975</span></a> <a href=\"#c23\" title=\"1 Dec 1975 · The Vale of Glamorgan becomes a compulsory registration area.\">C23 <span class=\"xd\">1 Dec 1975</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive.\">C25 <span class=\"xd\">23 Feb 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pending.\">C31 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1987</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c25\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C25</span><span class=\"dt\">23 Feb 1983</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse, WA240304, on Form 1C, while Mary is alive and living there <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0066-hmlr-wa240304-item-10-register-1983/\">EV-0066</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0063-hmlr-wa240304-item-11-form-1c/\">EV-0063</a>. The form requires the applicant to state that it is in possession <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0065-wa240304-farmhouse-first-registration-file/\">EV-0065</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0066-hmlr-wa240304-item-10-register-1983/\">EV-0066</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0063-hmlr-wa240304-item-11-form-1c/\">EV-0063</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0065-wa240304-farmhouse-first-registration-file/\">EV-0065</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and sewer \">C22 <span class=\"xd\">23 May 1975</span></a> <a href=\"#c23\" title=\"1 Dec 1975 · The Vale of Glamorgan becomes a compulsory registration area.\">C23 <span class=\"xd\">1 Dec 1975</span></a> <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required within two \">C24 <span class=\"xd\">19 and 30 Nov 1982</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c27\" title=\"8 Apr – 12 May 1983 · The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form D23), corres\">C27 <span class=\"xd\">8 Apr – 12 May 1983</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What did BP state about possession and the occupier? The application papers would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c26\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C26</span><span class=\"dt\">26 Mar 1983</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0067-mary-doreen-williams-death-index/\">EV-0067</a>; the family records an illness in the weeks before. BP&#x27;s 1974 undertaking ran &quot;until you personally no longer live there&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a>; in 1988 BP&#x27;s spokesman gave her death as the point when &quot;it became clear her son was not going to leave&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0067-mary-doreen-williams-death-index/\">EV-0067</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c27\" title=\"8 Apr – 12 May 1983 · The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form D23), corres\">C27 <span class=\"xd\">8 Apr – 12 May 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29 <span class=\"xd\">May 1984</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c27\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C27</span><span class=\"dt\">8 Apr – 12 May 1983</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form D23), correspondence of 12 Apr and letters of 12 May 1983.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The Registry examines the application after her death: Linklaters&#x27; letter of 8 Apr (form D23), correspondence of 12 Apr and letters of 12 May 1983 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0069-hmlr-wa240304-item-7-d23-1983/\">EV-0069</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0070-hmlr-wa240304-item-4-correspondence-1983/\">EV-0070</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0071-wa231076-1983-84-registration-activity/\">EV-0071</a>. The title takes effect from the application date.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0069-hmlr-wa240304-item-7-d23-1983/\">EV-0069</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0070-hmlr-wa240304-item-4-correspondence-1983/\">EV-0070</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0071-wa231076-1983-84-registration-activity/\">EV-0071</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive.\">C25 <span class=\"xd\">23 Feb 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c26\" title=\"26 Mar 1983 · Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).\">C26 <span class=\"xd\">26 Mar 1983</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pending.\">C31 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1987</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What did the 1983 letters tell the Registry about who lived in the house? The Registry copy file, due 28 Oct 2026, would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c28\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C28</span><span class=\"dt\">26 Jul 1983 (in force 1 Sep 1983)</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Commons Registration (Glamorgan) Act 1983 validates the Glamorgan common-land registers.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Parliament validates the Glamorgan common-land registers <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0232-commons-registration-glamorgan-act-1983/\">EV-0232</a>. The Act covers common land; VG41 is a village-green registration <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\">EV-0044</a>. No direct effect on the farmhouse has been found.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0232-commons-registration-glamorgan-act-1983/\">EV-0232</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\">EV-0044</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c16\" title=\"16 Jun 1970 · Village green VG41 registered by Glamorgan County Council.\">C16 <span class=\"xd\">16 Jun 1970</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Which 1983 step is meant here? If it is the farmhouse registration, see C25 and C27.</div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-8\">1984–1987</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c29\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C29</span><span class=\"dt\">May 1984</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The son is sued as occupier <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0073-family-solicitors-litigation-file-1984-87/\">EV-0073</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a>. The family is now the defendant.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0073-family-solicitors-litigation-file-1984-87/\">EV-0073</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c26\" title=\"26 Mar 1983 · Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).\">C26 <span class=\"xd\">26 Mar 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and sewer \">C22 <span class=\"xd\">23 May 1975</span></a> <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c30\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C30</span><span class=\"dt\">10–24 Jul 1986</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Judgment for BP: Frederick&#x27;s possession held not adverse, and the 1974 letters held to make Mary a licensee, so the limitation defence under the 1939 and 1980 Acts failed <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0074-high-court-trial-judgment-1986/\">EV-0074</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0075-south-wales-echo-1986-high-court-judgment/\">EV-0075</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0074-high-court-trial-judgment-1986/\">EV-0074</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0075-south-wales-echo-1986-high-court-judgment/\">EV-0075</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29 <span class=\"xd\">May 1984</span></a> <a href=\"#c14\" title=\"1965–67 · Frederick Buckler dies. Mary stays in the house.\">C14 <span class=\"xd\">1965–67</span></a> <a href=\"#c12\" title=\"1959 and Mar 1965 · Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing is offere\">C12 <span class=\"xd\">1959 and Mar 1965</span></a> <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c21\" title=\"Nov–Dec 1974 · On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not reject\">C21 <span class=\"xd\">Nov–Dec 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pending.\">C31 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1987</span></a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c31\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C31</span><span class=\"dt\">2 Feb 1987</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pending.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title, WA231076 item 14, while the appeal is pending <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0078-1987-title-amalgamation-application-plan/\">EV-0078</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0078-1987-title-amalgamation-application-plan/\">EV-0078</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c27\" title=\"8 Apr – 12 May 1983 · The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form D23), corres\">C27 <span class=\"xd\">8 Apr – 12 May 1983</span></a> <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required within two \">C24 <span class=\"xd\">19 and 30 Nov 1982</span></a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c36\" title=\"9 Jul 1988 · Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.\">C36 <span class=\"xd\">9 Jul 1988</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What class of title was granted in 1983? If possessory, the rules from 1 Jan 1987 on upgrading during an open adverse claim would apply. The register would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c32\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C32</span><span class=\"dt\">31 Jul 1987</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; leave to appeal to the House of Lords refused.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The appeal is dismissed; possession in six weeks; leave to appeal to the House of Lords refused <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. The court accepted adverse possession by Frederick and Mary from 1955 and held that the 1962 order and the 1974 letters defeated it.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30 <span class=\"xd\">10–24 Jul 1986</span></a> <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l\">C20 <span class=\"xd\">31 Oct 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c21\" title=\"Nov–Dec 1974 · On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not reject\">C21 <span class=\"xd\">Nov–Dec 1974</span></a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit\">C13 <span class=\"xd\">11 Dec 1962</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c33\" title=\"1987–88 · Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.\">C33 <span class=\"xd\">1987–88</span></a> <a href=\"#c34\" title=\"3 May 1988 · Application to the European Commission of Human Rights (14464/88), later declared inadmissible.\">C34 <span class=\"xd\">3 May 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c35\" title=\"Apr–May 1988 · First eviction attempt; BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press.\">C35 <span class=\"xd\">Apr–May 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c36\" title=\"9 Jul 1988 · Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.\">C36 <span class=\"xd\">9 Jul 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital \">C38 <span class=\"xd\">30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c39\" title=\"6 Dec 1988 · The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.\">C39 <span class=\"xd\">6 Dec 1988</span></a></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"period-9\">1988</h2>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c33\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C33</span><span class=\"dt\">1987–88</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> A petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords is lodged <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0076-house-of-lords-petition-leave-papers/\">EV-0076</a>. The outcome papers are not yet held.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0076-house-of-lords-petition-leave-papers/\">EV-0076</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c34\" title=\"3 May 1988 · Application to the European Commission of Human Rights (14464/88), later declared inadmissible.\">C34 <span class=\"xd\">3 May 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital \">C38 <span class=\"xd\">30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What became of the petition? The House of Lords Journal would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c34\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C34</span><span class=\"dt\">3 May 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Application to the European Commission of Human Rights (14464/88), later declared inadmissible.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Application 14464/88 to the European Commission of Human Rights is declared inadmissible, so there is no hearing on the merits <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0122-echr-application-14464-88-inadmissibility/\">EV-0122</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0122-echr-application-14464-88-inadmissibility/\">EV-0122</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a> <a href=\"#c33\" title=\"1987–88 · Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.\">C33 <span class=\"xd\">1987–88</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c35\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C35</span><span class=\"dt\">Apr–May 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">First eviction attempt; BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The first eviction attempt is reported <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0089-chainsaw-farmer-vows-fight-on/\">EV-0089</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0090-south-wales-echo-bailiffs-medical-attention/\">EV-0090</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0092-echo-alun-michael-lord-chancellor/\">EV-0092</a>; BP&#x27;s spokesman sets out BP&#x27;s account of the case <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a>. The word &quot;squatters&quot; is a label others applied to the family.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0089-chainsaw-farmer-vows-fight-on/\">EV-0089</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0090-south-wales-echo-bailiffs-medical-attention/\">EV-0090</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0092-echo-alun-michael-lord-chancellor/\">EV-0092</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c37\" title=\"29 Jul – Dec 1988 · Cadw inspects and photographs the house; the listing decision comes in December 1988.\">C37 <span class=\"xd\">29 Jul – Dec 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital \">C38 <span class=\"xd\">30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c36\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C36</span><span class=\"dt\">9 Jul 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The Estates Gazette reports BP planning sales in Wales <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0093-estates-gazette-1988-bp-welsh-sales/\">EV-0093</a>. No record yet ties the 1982–83 filings to a sale.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0093-estates-gazette-1988-bp-welsh-sales/\">EV-0093</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a> <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pending.\">C31 <span class=\"xd\">2 Feb 1987</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c40\" title=\"7 Dec 1988 · The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).\">C40 <span class=\"xd\">7 Dec 1988</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> Was the farm part of the 1988 sale? Sale particulars or the Land Registry history would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c37\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C37</span><span class=\"dt\">29 Jul – Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Cadw inspects and photographs the house; the listing decision comes in December 1988.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Cadw inspects and photographs the house in July 1988 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0094-cadw-barn-survey-photo-1988/\">EV-0094</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0095-cadw-farmhouse-survey-photo-1988/\">EV-0095</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0096-cadw-1988-inspection-photographs-listing/\">EV-0096</a>; the listing decision is dated December 1988 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0103-echo-history-fight-save-farm/\">EV-0103</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0094-cadw-barn-survey-photo-1988/\">EV-0094</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0095-cadw-farmhouse-survey-photo-1988/\">EV-0095</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0096-cadw-1988-inspection-photographs-listing/\">EV-0096</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0103-echo-history-fight-save-farm/\">EV-0103</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c35\" title=\"Apr–May 1988 · First eviction attempt; BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press.\">C35 <span class=\"xd\">Apr–May 1988</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c40\" title=\"7 Dec 1988 · The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).\">C40 <span class=\"xd\">7 Dec 1988</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> When did Cadw&#x27;s decision reach BP and the council? The listing file would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c38\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C38</span><span class=\"dt\">30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital bed to face an assault charge.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> Forced entry, the outbuilding roof removed and the residents evicted <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0098-south-wales-echo-forced-entry-1988/\">EV-0098</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0099-south-wales-echo-bp-summons-1988/\">EV-0099</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0101-echo-extract-hospital-assault-charges/\">EV-0101</a>; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital bed to face an assault charge <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0102-billys-unhappy-family-echo-1988/\">EV-0102</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0098-south-wales-echo-forced-entry-1988/\">EV-0098</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0099-south-wales-echo-bp-summons-1988/\">EV-0099</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0101-echo-extract-hospital-assault-charges/\">EV-0101</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0102-billys-unhappy-family-echo-1988/\">EV-0102</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a> <a href=\"#c33\" title=\"1987–88 · Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.\">C33 <span class=\"xd\">1987–88</span></a> <a href=\"#c35\" title=\"Apr–May 1988 · First eviction attempt; BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press.\">C35 <span class=\"xd\">Apr–May 1988</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c39\" title=\"6 Dec 1988 · The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.\">C39 <span class=\"xd\">6 Dec 1988</span></a></div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Open question:</b> What became of the assault charge? The magistrates&#x27; record would answer it.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c39\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C39</span><span class=\"dt\">6 Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The application at the Cardiff High Court fails <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0104-south-wales-echo-extract-1988/\">EV-0104</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0105-western-mail-final-eviction-hearing-1988/\">EV-0105</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0104-south-wales-echo-extract-1988/\">EV-0104</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0105-western-mail-final-eviction-hearing-1988/\">EV-0105</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital \">C38 <span class=\"xd\">30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; \">C32 <span class=\"xd\">31 Jul 1987</span></a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c40\" title=\"7 Dec 1988 · The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).\">C40 <span class=\"xd\">7 Dec 1988</span></a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c40\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C40</span><span class=\"dt\">7 Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press, SMR)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>What changed:</b> The farmhouse is demolished <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0106-tears-flow-farmhouse-razed-1988/\">EV-0106</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0107-south-wales-echo-1988-councillor-protest/\">EV-0107</a>. The Sites and Monuments Record later enters &quot;building destroyed by owners&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0108-south-wales-echo-bp-demolition-anger/\">EV-0108</a>.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0106-tears-flow-farmhouse-razed-1988/\">EV-0106</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0107-south-wales-echo-1988-councillor-protest/\">EV-0107</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0108-south-wales-echo-bp-demolition-anger/\">EV-0108</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c39\" title=\"6 Dec 1988 · The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.\">C39 <span class=\"xd\">6 Dec 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c37\" title=\"29 Jul – Dec 1988 · Cadw inspects and photographs the house; the listing decision comes in December 1988.\">C37 <span class=\"xd\">29 Jul – Dec 1988</span></a> <a href=\"#c36\" title=\"9 Jul 1988 · Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.\">C36 <span class=\"xd\">9 Jul 1988</span></a></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"after\">After 7 December 1988</h2><ul class=\"tight\">\n<li><b>11 Feb 1989</b>: Vale councillors authorise legal action against BP Properties over the demolition. <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0117-south-wales-echo-1989-vale-legal-action/\">EV-0117</a></li>\n<li><b>Mar 1989</b>: Sites and Monuments Record PRN 02038s: &quot;building destroyed by owners&quot;. <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0118-smr-record-card-1989-building-destroyed/\">EV-0118</a></li>\n<li><b>13 Mar 1990</b>: Outline planning permission for houses at Great House Farm (89/01396/OUT). <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0124-outline-planning-permission-89-01396-out-residenti/\">EV-0124</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0114-planning-report-89-01396-out-outline-permission/\">EV-0114</a></li>\n<li><b>1992–94</b>: Reserved matters approved and 20 houses built. <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0127-planning-application-form-d-for-approval-of-reserv/\">EV-0127</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0129-approved-planning-drawings-ref-92-00671-res-screen/\">EV-0129</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0133-planning-drawings-ideal-homes-wales-llandough-farm/\">EV-0133</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"ingredients\">What the record shows was decided</h2><ul class=\"tight\"><li>Jul 1955: possession of the whole farm except the farmhouse and garden, under a High Court order <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> (the order itself is not yet located). See <a href=\"#c10\">C10</a>.</li><li>11 Dec 1962: possession of the farmhouse and garden, Cardiff County Court <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a>. See <a href=\"#c13\">C13</a>.</li><li>Sep 1974: leave to execute the 1962 order <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a>. See <a href=\"#c19\">C19</a>.</li><li>Jul 1986: judgment for BP; Frederick&#x27;s possession not adverse; Mary a licensee from the 31 Oct 1974 letters <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0074-high-court-trial-judgment-1986/\">EV-0074</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0075-south-wales-echo-1986-high-court-judgment/\">EV-0075</a>. See <a href=\"#c30\">C30</a>.</li><li>31 Jul 1987: appeal dismissed; the 1962 order stopped the clock before 12 years; from the 1974 letters possession was no longer adverse; adverse possession from 1955 accepted; leave to appeal to the House of Lords refused <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. See <a href=\"#c32\">C32</a>.</li><li>1988: the human-rights application declared inadmissible <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0122-echr-application-14464-88-inadmissibility/\">EV-0122</a>, and the final eviction hearing of 6 Dec 1988 failed <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0104-south-wales-echo-extract-1988/\">EV-0104</a>. See <a href=\"#c34\">C34</a> and <a href=\"#c39\">C39</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"undecided\">What was never decided</h2><ul class=\"tight\"><li>The 3 Jul 1974 plea that BP&#x27;s claim was barred by adverse possession: adjourned part-heard and, in the Court of Appeal&#x27;s words, &quot;has never been finally heard&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. See <a href=\"#c18\">C18</a>.</li><li>No court decision on the record determines who owned the farmhouse as a question of title; the 1986 and 1987 judgments decided possession and limitation <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0075-south-wales-echo-1986-high-court-judgment/\">EV-0075</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</li><li>No record of compensation for the demolition, and no finding against any party for it, has been located. The outcome of the Vale councillors&#x27; 1989 decision to take legal action <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0117-south-wales-echo-1989-vale-legal-action/\">EV-0117</a> is not yet located.</li><li>The House of Lords outcome papers are not yet held <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0076-house-of-lords-petition-leave-papers/\">EV-0076</a>. See <a href=\"#c33\">C33</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"against\">What the courts found against the family</h2><ul class=\"tight\"><li>The Court of Appeal held that the 1962 order stopped the 12-year period before it ran, and that from the 1974 letters Mary&#x27;s possession was no longer adverse <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. These holdings stand unless set aside.</li><li>The judgment records rent arrears in the 1930s and 1940s and a last payment in 1953 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>, against the family&#x27;s account of rent ending in 1928 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a>.</li><li>The trial judge found that Frederick had no intention to possess as owner, relying on the March 1965 offer <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. See <a href=\"#c12\">C12</a>.</li><li>BP did not depend on the 1983 registration to sue: the 1984 action succeeded on the 1974 letters <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0073-family-solicitors-litigation-file-1984-87/\">EV-0073</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</li><li>No record yet shows BP knew of Mary&#x27;s final illness, or that the 1983 filing was timed to it.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"open\">Open questions</h2><ul class=\"tight\"><li>What does the 1974 Cardiff County Court file show was pleaded and left undecided? The HMCTS reply due 2 Nov 2026 would show it <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a>.</li><li>What did BP and its solicitors tell the Land Registry in 1983 about who lived in the house? The application papers and the 8 Apr, 12 Apr and 12 May 1983 letters (Registry reply due 28 Oct 2026) would show it <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0069-hmlr-wa240304-item-7-d23-1983/\">EV-0069</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0070-hmlr-wa240304-item-4-correspondence-1983/\">EV-0070</a>.</li><li>Did Mary or her solicitors reject the licence after 31 Oct 1974 in writing? A letter doing so would meet the point the Court of Appeal identified <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</li><li>Was the farmhouse parcel inside the 1938 Bute–Western Ground Rents conveyance and plan <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0019-bute-wgr-conveyance-plan-1938/\">EV-0019</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0023-1939-wgr-john-williams-tenancy-plan/\">EV-0023</a>?</li><li>Each &quot;Open question&quot; line in the entries above is a further ingredient still missing.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"theories\">Competing theories, most plausible first</h2>\n<p>Competing theories that could account for the entries above, ordered from most to least plausible given all the evidence held today: how much of the record each accounts for, and how much stands against it. Each is a theory, not a finding. The courts&#x27; view is included and ranked like the others.</p>\n<div class=\"cut thy\" id=\"t1\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">T1</span><span class=\"lab l-inf\">Theory 1 of 5</span></div><div class=\"ev\"><b>The courts&#x27; view: possession was lawfully recovered and the paper title was never extinguished.</b> The family held as tenants until the 1955 notice to quit, then as adverse possessors; the 1962 order stopped the 12-year period before it ran, and the 31 Oct 1974 letters made Mary&#x27;s later possession a licence, so the paper title running from Bute through the 1938 conveyance to BP was never extinguished and possession was recovered lawfully.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence for:</b> The 1916 tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a>; the 1953 rent payment under a judgment <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>; the 1962 possession order <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a>; the 1974 letters <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a>; the High Court judgment <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0075-south-wales-echo-1986-high-court-judgment/\">EV-0075</a> and the Court of Appeal <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>. These holdings bind unless set aside.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence against:</b> The 1974 adverse-possession plea &quot;has never been finally heard&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a>; the family&#x27;s account of rent ending in 1928 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a>; the 1939 plan shows only the fields <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0023-1939-wgr-john-williams-tenancy-plan/\">EV-0023</a>; whether the 1938 conveyance included the farmhouse parcel has not been read <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0019-bute-wgr-conveyance-plan-1938/\">EV-0019</a>.</div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Would be confirmed or refuted by:</b> Confirmed by a 1938 conveyance plan that includes the farmhouse parcel and by the absence of any written rejection of the 1974 licence. Refuted by a plan that leaves the farmhouse out, or a letter rejecting the licence after 31 Oct 1974.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut thy\" id=\"t2\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">T2</span><span class=\"lab l-inf\">Theory 2 of 5</span></div><div class=\"ev\"><b>Lawful steps, sequenced against the limitation clock.</b> Each step was lawful on its own, but together they kept the family&#x27;s possession from ever running its 12 years, without the ownership plea being decided: the 1962 order, its revival about 12 weeks before the period from it ended, the licence letters, and the 1983 registration while Mary was alive.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence for:</b> Leave to execute in Sep 1974 against an 11 Dec 1974 expiry <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>; the letters of 31 Oct 1974 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a>; the undecided 1974 plea <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a>; the 1983 application made in her lifetime <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0066-hmlr-wa240304-item-10-register-1983/\">EV-0066</a>; BP&#x27;s spokesman in 1988 on waiting until her death <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a>.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence against:</b> Waiting for her death is also what the 1974 letters promised <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a>; the 1982 field registration was compulsory <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0265-hmlr-registration-background-compulsory-1975-r29-certificate/\">EV-0265</a>; BP&#x27;s 1984 action succeeded on the 1974 letters, not on the 1983 registration <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>; no record yet shows BP knew of her final illness.</div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Would be confirmed or refuted by:</b> Confirmed or refuted by the 1974 Cardiff County Court file (HMCTS reply due 2 Nov 2026) <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a> and BP&#x27;s own files on the 1974 and 1983 steps.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut thy\" id=\"t3\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">T3</span><span class=\"lab l-inf\">Theory 3 of 5</span></div><div class=\"ev\"><b>The farmhouse parcel stood outside the paper chain.</b> Parcel A, the house parcel, was never conveyed in the Bute → Western Ground Rents chain, so the possession cases started from a paper title that did not cover the house.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence for:</b> The 1939 agreement plan highlights the fields only <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0023-1939-wgr-john-williams-tenancy-plan/\">EV-0023</a>; the family&#x27;s account of the house standing apart <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a>; the separate 1983 registration of the farmhouse <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0066-hmlr-wa240304-item-10-register-1983/\">EV-0066</a>.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence against:</b> The 1916 tenancy covers &quot;the whole of the farm&quot; with plan <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a>; the courts took the paper title to the farm as their starting point <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>; the 1938 conveyance and its plan have not yet been read <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0019-bute-wgr-conveyance-plan-1938/\">EV-0019</a>.</div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Would be confirmed or refuted by:</b> Settled either way by the 1938 Bute–Western Ground Rents conveyance and plan, and the 1905 Bute conveyance.</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut thy\" id=\"t4\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">T4</span><span class=\"lab l-inf\">Theory 4 of 5</span></div><div class=\"ev\"><b>The 1983 registration misdescribed the occupation.</b> BP&#x27;s 1983 application for the farmhouse, made while Mary lived there and examined after her death, did not tell the Registry the true position of the occupier.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence for:</b> The application date and her death in the weeks after it <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0066-hmlr-wa240304-item-10-register-1983/\">EV-0066</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0067-mary-doreen-williams-death-index/\">EV-0067</a>; the 8 Apr, 12 Apr and 12 May 1983 letters exist <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0069-hmlr-wa240304-item-7-d23-1983/\">EV-0069</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0070-hmlr-wa240304-item-4-correspondence-1983/\">EV-0070</a> <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0071-wa231076-1983-84-registration-activity/\">EV-0071</a>; the house title was merged into the farm title while the appeal was pending <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0078-1987-title-amalgamation-application-plan/\">EV-0078</a>.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence against:</b> What the letters say is not yet known; registration times in 1982–83 were ordinary; the 1984 action did not depend on the registration <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a>.</div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Would be confirmed or refuted by:</b> Confirmed or refuted by the Land Registry&#x27;s 1983 application papers and letters (reply due 28 Oct 2026).</div></div>\n<div class=\"cut thy\" id=\"t5\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">T5</span><span class=\"lab l-inf\">Theory 5 of 5</span></div><div class=\"ev\"><b>A 1988 sale drove the clearance.</b> The site had become an asset for sale in 1988, and the clearance served that sale.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence for:</b> &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;, Estates Gazette, 9 Jul 1988 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0093-estates-gazette-1988-bp-welsh-sales/\">EV-0093</a>; the 1975 deed reserved road and sewer rights &quot;to serve any development&quot; <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0052-bp-pension-trust-bp-properties-conveyance/\">EV-0052</a>; houses followed from 1990 <a class=\"ev-l\" href=\"/evidence/ev-0124-outline-planning-permission-89-01396-out-residenti/\">EV-0124</a>.</div><div class=\"chg\"><b>Evidence against:</b> No record ties the farm to the 1988 sale; the land was still being sold off by BP Properties in 1989 and 1993; the 1986 charge to Intercontinental was over a London office, not Llandough.</div><div class=\"opn\"><b>Would be confirmed or refuted by:</b> Sale particulars for 1988–93, or the Land Registry history of WA231076.</div></div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Version 2.1.0, 2026-10-25. Each entry is one row in the catalogue database, with its evidence links and cross-links. <a href=\"#tc-top\">Back to top</a></p>\n</div>"}};
